      "text": [
        "هَا أَبْوَالُ اَلدَّوَابِّ وَ اَلسِّرْجِينُ وَ يَدْخُلُهَا اَلْيَهُودُ وَ اَلنَّصَارَى كَيْفَ نَصْنَعُ بِالصَّلاَةِ فِيهَا فَقَالَ «صَلِّ عَلَى ثَوْبِكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.733 - Amir ibn Nuaym al-Qummi asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about places where people stay that contain the urine of animals, manure, and are frequented by Jews and Christians.\nHe asked: \"What should we do about praying in such places?\"\nAbu 'Abdillah replied: \"Pray on your garment.\""
        ]
      }
